# UF Scheduling Assistant — Project Context

## Purpose
LLM-powered FastAPI microservice that helps UF students research courses. Aggregates data from four sources: UF One.UF Schedule of Courses API (live), RateMyProfessors (GraphQL), r/UFL Reddit posts (local JSON + live scrape), and (planned) GatorEvals.

## Architecture

```
main.py                       (FastAPI app + lifespan — uvicorn main:app)
api/                          (API package)
  __init__.py
  routers/
    __init__.py               (aggregates all sub-routers)
    health.py                 (GET /health)
    chat.py                   (POST /chat, DELETE /chat/{session_id})
    chat_room.py              (SSE events, send/load messages)
    metrics.py                (POST major/course/search tracking)
    user.py                   (user routes — stub)
  controllers/
    chat.py                   (AI chat business logic, SSE streaming)
    chat_room.py              (pub/sub chat room, DynamoDB persistence)
    metrics.py                (daily analytics counters)
    user.py                   (user management — stub)
  models/
    __init__.py               (re-exports all Pydantic models)
    chat.py                   (ChatRequest, ChatDeleteResponse)
    health.py                 (HealthResponse)
    chat_room.py              (SendMessageRequest)
    metrics.py                (TrackMajorRequest, TrackCourseRequest, …)
    user.py                   (user models — stub)
sessions.py                   (in-memory session store keyed by UUID hex)
chat.py                       (build_agent() — LangGraph ReAct agent + tools)
  └── tools/                  (@tool-decorated LangChain tool functions)
        ├── course_search.py → course_data.py (UF SOC live API)
        ├── rmp_search.py     (RateMyProfessors GraphQL)
        └── reddit_search.py  (local JSON + live Reddit API)
utils/auth.py                 (Cognito JWT validation via python-jose)
constants.py                  (env-driven config)
dynamo.py                     (DynamoDB table references)
scrapers/                     (offline ETL — NOT part of the live request path)
```

## API Endpoints

| Method | Path | Auth | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| `GET` | `/health` | None | `{"status": "ok"}` |
| `POST` | `/chat` | Bearer JWT | Accepts `ChatRequest`; returns SSE stream |
| `DELETE` | `/chat/{session_id}` | Bearer JWT | Deletes a session |
| `GET` | `/chat-room/events` | Bearer JWT | SSE stream of chat room messages + active users |
| `POST` | `/chat-room/messages` | Bearer JWT | Send a chat room message |
| `GET` | `/chat-room/messages` | None | Paginated message history |
| `POST` | `/metrics/major` | None | Track major selection |
| `POST` | `/metrics/course` | None | Track course view |
| `POST` | `/metrics/search` | None | Track search term |

SSE event format:
```
event: token    data: {"token": "...", "session_id": "abc"}
event: done     data: {"session_id": "abc"}
event: error    data: {"detail": "..."}
```

## Key Conventions

- **Thin routes, fat controller:** routers in `api/routers/` are one-liners; all logic lives in `api/controllers/`
- **`from __future__ import annotations`** in every module
- **Tool outputs are plain text strings** — not JSON — so the LLM can interpret them directly
- **Global agent singleton:** `api.controllers.chat.agent` is `None` at import time, set during FastAPI `lifespan`; never re-initialized per request
- **Lazy session pruning:** `_prune_expired()` runs on every `create_session` / `get_session` call
- **Sessions scoped to user `sub`** (Cognito subject claim) — a session belongs to one user

## Environment Variables (from `.env` via `constants.py`)

| Variable | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `OPENAI_API_KEY` | OpenAI key (`gpt-4o-mini`) |
| `COGNITO_REGION` | AWS region of Cognito user pool |
| `COGNITO_USER_POOL_ID` | Cognito User Pool ID |
| `COGNITO_APP_CLIENT_ID` | JWT audience |
| `ALLOWED_ORIGINS` | Comma-separated CORS origins (default `"*"`) |

Hardcoded: `SESSION_TTL_SECONDS = 1800`, `JWKS_TTL_SECONDS = 3600`, UF SOC base URL `https://one.ufl.edu/apix/soc/schedule/`

## Data Models

**`ChatRequest`** (Pydantic, `api/models/chat.py`):
```python
prompt: str
session_id: str | None = None
```

**`_Session`** (internal dataclass, `sessions.py`):
```python
user_sub: str
messages: list[dict[str, str]]  # {"role": "user"|"assistant", "content": str}
last_active: float               # time.monotonic()
```

**UF course dict** keys: `code`, `codeWithSpace`, `name`, `description`, `prerequisites`, `sections[]`  
Each section: `number`, `classNumber`, `sectWeb` (delivery mode), `instructors[]`, `meetTimes[]`, `credits_min`, `credits_max`, `genEd[]`, `quest[]`, `openSeats`, `waitList`, `courseFee`, `finalExam`, `note`, `deptName`

**Reddit post dict** keys: `id`, `title`, `selftext`, `author`, `created_utc`, `score`, `num_comments`, `flair`, `permalink`, `url`, `comments[]`

## Important Design Decisions

- **Live UF API:** `course_data.py` always queries `one.ufl.edu` in real time — no local course cache. Static JSON snapshots from the old scraper (`UF_Feb-11-2026_26_spring_clean.json`) are deleted/deprecated.
- **Reddit:** Posts are stored in a SQLite database (`scrapers/reddit_scrapes/master/UFL_reddit.db`) and searched via FTS5 by `tools/reddit_search.py`.
- **In-memory sessions:** Explicitly not suitable for multi-container deployments. A comment in `sessions.py` calls this out — Redis or DynamoDB is the recommended drop-in replacement.
- **JWKS rotation recovery:** If a `kid` is missing from the cache, `utils/auth.py` force-refreshes once before failing.
- **Vulgarity filtering:** `reddit_search.py` applies a compiled regex word-boundary filter before returning Reddit content to the LLM.
- **Term auto-detection:** `course_data.py` maps current month → UF term code (`Spring=1-4`, `Summer=5-7`, `Fall=8-12`) encoded as `2{YY}{sem}` (e.g. Spring 2026 = `"2261"`).
- **`chat.py` doubles as a CLI:** `main()` provides a terminal loop for quick local testing without running the full API.

## Scrapers (offline ETL — do not modify unless working on data pipeline)

- `scrapers/ufcoursecatalog.py` — bulk download UF SOC API → `_clean.json`
- `scrapers/reddit_flair_scraper.py` — scrapes r/UFL by flair (Classes, Schedule, Graduation) → `UFL_master.json`
- `scrapers/run_reddit_scrapes.py` — orchestrator for `initial` (50-day backfill) / `daily` (3-day) modes; tracks state in `reddit_scrapes/state/daily_progress.json`

## Deployment

Dockerfile: Python 3.12-slim, port 8000, health check on `/health`, `uvicorn main:app`  
Makefile targets: `make build`, `make run`, `make run-mount` (dev with volume), `make stop`
